B.a6i=new A.f(323,"caution","DO THE ECG - THIS IS THE LINE THAT KILLS IF IT IS SKIPPED - an ECG is a cornerstone of the work-up, there to exclude a cardiac cause that would matter. The article names long QT syndrome among the conditions to rule out, and asks that the other causes of a faint or a fit be excluded too - epilepsy and the arrhythmias. A pallid spell, an episode with no crying, one during exercise or swimming, or a family history of sudden death or deafness makes the ECG urgent.")
