B.axn=new A.h("candidiasis-of-nails","Itraconazole","Child nail disease: specialist assessment for immune disease; no sourced nail-treatment dose.","oral.solid",'SPORANOX (itraconazole) Capsules US prescribing information, DailyMed set id a4d555fa-787c-40fb-bb7d-b0d4f7318fd0, revised 7/2026, DOSAGE AND ADMINISTRATION - verbatim: "Toenails with or without fingernail involvement The recommended dose is 200 mg (2 capsules) once daily for 12 consecutive weeks." and "Fingernails only The recommended dosing regimen is 2 treatment pulses, each consisting of 200 mg (2 capsules) b.i.d. (400 mg/day) for 1 week. The pulses are separated by a 3-week period without SPORANOX." The Egyptian formulary gives the same two schedules - Egyptian National Drug Formulary 2023 - Antimicrobial (Version 1.0), itraconazole monograph (formulary page 45) - verbatim: "Onychomycosis: Note: Other agents are preferred for dermatophyte onychomycosis. Oral: Capsule or tablet: Continuous dosing: 200 mg once daily for 6 weeks or 12 weeks. Pulsed dosing: 200 mg twice daily for 1 week; repeat every 4 weeks for 2 months or 3 months".',"Oral azole for a culture-confirmed candidal nail","200 mg once daily for 12 weeks where a toenail is involved; for fingernails only, 200 mg twice daily for 1 week, repeated after 3 weeks without it","12 weeks continuous for toenails, or 2 one-week pulses for fingernails",u.ql)
B.aAb=new A.h("cardiac-arrest","Adrenaline","Pediatric resuscitation algorithm/team; no cardiac-arrest dose in the held sources. Bradycardia dosing is a different indication.","injection",u.gn,"Resuscitation",u.EC,u.Y,u.zL)
B.avN=new A.h("cardiovascular-infection","Ceftriaxone","Urgent pediatric admission; no sourced child endocarditis amount. Receiving team determines treatment.","injection",u.KY,"Streptococcal endocarditis",u.ON,u.s,u.YG)
B.ayy=new A.h("chalazion","Tobramycin","Secondary bacterial infection only; age \u22652 months, mild/moderate: 1\u20132 drops of 0.3% tobramycin into affected eye(s) every 4 h.","eye",'Tobramycin Ophthalmic Solution USP 0.3%, DOSAGE AND ADMINISTRATION (DailyMed SetID 3c23234a-452b-40d0-922f-37e49147d537, Alembic Pharmaceuticals): "In mild to moderate disease, instill 1 or 2 drops into the affected eye(s) every 4 hours. In severe infections, instill 2 drops into the eye(s) hourly until improvement, following which treatment should be reduced prior to discontinuation." The same label sets no separate paediatric dose - see peds_note.',null,"In mild to moderate disease, instill one or two drops into the affected eye(s) every four hours.",null,u.Ps)
B.aDc=new A.h("childhood-food-allergy","Cetirizine","Oral, after adrenaline if needed for itch/urticaria: 2\u20136 years 2.5 mg once/twice daily; 6\u201312 years 5 mg twice daily or 10 mg daily; >12 years 10 mg daily. No oral dose below 2.","oral.liquid","Egyptian National Drug Formulary - Respiratory 2026 (cetirizine monograph, p13)","If itch or urticaria needs relief after adrenaline: add cetirizine","10 mg once daily by mouth","While symptoms last",u.JZ)
B.aDY=new A.h("chondromalacia-patellae","Paracetamol",u.u,"oral.solid",u.m,null,u.U,"As needed for pain or fever",u.o)
B.aBe=new A.h("coma","Glucose (dextrose)","Hypoglycaemia: 10% glucose, 2 mL/kg by slow IV injection; urgent transfer/recheck glucose. Do not use 50% directly in children.","injection",'MSF Essential Drugs 2024, GLUCOSE 50% = DEXTROSE 50% injectable - verbatim: "Adult: 1 ml/kg by slow IV injection"',"Emergency reversal of hypoglycaemia","50% glucose (500 mg/mL) 1 mL/kg by slow intravenous injection over 3 to 5 minutes",null,u.qE)
B.awS=new A.h("corneal-abrasion","Ofloxacin",u.S1,"eye","Exocin 3 mg/ml Eye Drops SmPC section 4.2 (eMC product 1353)","Contact lens wearer - Pseudomonas cover","1-2 drops into the affected eye every 2-4 hours for the first 2 days, then 4 times daily. Never longer than 10 days.","5-7 days, maximum 10",u.EK)
