B.avg=new A.h("nipple-discharge-referral","Diagnostic Assessment and Referral","Benign neonatal milk discharge: reassure, do not squeeze. Adolescent discharge: pediatric endocrine/gynaecology assessment.",null,"NICE Guideline NG12: Suspected cancer: recognition and referral 2015",null,"Refer using a suspected cancer pathway referral for breast cancer if aged 50 and over with discharge, retraction, or other changes of concern in 1 nipple only.","Urgent evaluation and referral",u.N2)
B.HM=new A.h("nose-symptoms","Fluticasone","Choose product-specific nasal regimen: furoate/propionate strengths and age limits differ; do not interchange dosing or infer escalation.","spray",u.OS,null,"Two spray actuations into each nostril once daily (110 mcg/day total if using the fluticasone furoate 27.5 mcg/spray product, or 200 mcg/day total if using the fluticasone propionate 50 mcg/spray product).","As directed",u.OZ)
B.HK=new A.h("omphalitis","Flucloxacillin","Urgent neonatal/hospital care; flucloxacillin needs its own day-of-life regimen. MSF cloxacillin figures are not automatically interchangeable.","injection",'Egyptian National Drug Formulary 2023 - Antimicrobial (flucloxacillin monograph, p351) - verbatim: "neonates: 25 mg/kg orally orintravenously, given twice daily for those under 7 days of age, 3 times daily for those 7 to 20 days of age, and 4 times daily for those 21 to 28 days of age; intravenous doses may be doubled for severe infection"; and MSF Essential Drugs 2024 (CLOXACILLIN injectable monograph, p383, whose indication line names omphalitis) - verbatim: "Neonate: 0 to 7 days (< 2 kg): 50 mg/kg every 12 hours 0 to 7 days (\u2265 2 kg): 50 mg/kg every 8 hours 8 days to < 1 month (< 2 kg): 50 mg/kg every 8 hours 8 days to < 1 month (\u2265 2 kg): 50 mg/kg every 6 hours"',null,"Not applicable - omphalitis is an illness of the newborn; the amounts are the neonatal ones in the age band","10 days parenteral in an uncomplicated case, then oral according to the cultures",u._I)
B.ayY=new A.h("oral-candidiasis","Miconazole","Oral gel after meals, four times daily: 4\u201324 months 1.25 mL; \u22652 years 2.5 mL. Split infant doses into small portions; never place at throat back.","topical","Daktarin Sugar Free 2% Oral Gel SmPC section 4.2 (eMC product 6597)","Oral gel - the option for angular cheilitis and denture stomatitis","2.5 ml of the 2% gel four times a day after meals, held in the mouth as long as possible before swallowing","Keep going a week or more beyond the point where the mouth looks clear",u._X)
