B.ayj=new A.h("precocious-puberty","Triptorelin","Confirmed central precocious puberty: specialist, product-specific depot regimen; weight/injection dates determine dosing. Do not substitute depot formulations.","injection",'GONAPEPTYL DEPOT 3.75 mg Powder and solvent for suspension for injection - Summary of Product Characteristics, eMC product 2229, sections 4.1 and 4.2 - https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/2229/smpc - verbatim: "Dosing at the beginning of treatment should be based on body weight, one injection of triptorelin should be injected on days 0, 14, and 28. Thereafter one injection every 4 weeks. Should the effect be insufficient, the injections may be given every 3 weeks." The licensed indication, section 4.1 - verbatim: "Treatment of confirmed central precocious puberty (girls under 9 years, boys under 10 years)".',"GnRH analogue depot - a paediatric endocrinologist starts it","Not applicable - central precocious puberty is treated in childhood (see the paediatric dose)","Repeated every 4 weeks until bone maturation passes 12 years in a girl or 13 years in a boy",u.SU)
B.aDA=new A.h("premature-ejaculation","Sertraline","Not for this indication under 18; pediatric OCD exception does not apply.","oral.solid","Premature Ejaculation - disease-level clinical article (premature-ejaculation-full.txt)",null,"50 to 200 mg/day",null,u.iD)
B.aBS=new A.h("preschool-viral-wheeze","Salbutamol","Rescue MDI: 2\u20134 puffs through spacer; repeat after 20 min. No bronchiolitis use in infants \u22641 year; incomplete response needs medical advice.","oral.inhalation","Preschool viral wheeze (paediatric asthma) - disease-level clinical article (preschool-viral-wheeze-full.txt)",null,"Not applicable - preschool viral wheeze is by definition a condition of children under 6 (see paediatric dosing)","As needed during an episode; reassess if needed more than twice a week",u.us)
B.auP=new A.h("prostatitis","Ofloxacin","Not for pediatric prostatitis; general susceptible-infection dosing is a different indication.","oral.solid","Egyptian National Drug Formulary - Antimicrobial 2023 (ofloxacin monograph, Indications naming Prostatitis and Dosage Regimen, Dosing: Adult usual adult dose), with the 2-to-4-week course from Acute Bacterial Prostatitis - disease-level clinical article (prostatitis-full.txt)","Oral fluoroquinolone - alternative to ciprofloxacin","200 to 400 mg every 12 hours","2 to 4 weeks",u.I2)
B.aCx=new A.h("rabies","Rabies immune globulin (human)","Category III, never vaccinated: human RIG 20 IU/kg at any age, infiltrated into wounds; do not exceed total. Rabies-centre care.","injection","WHO. Rabies vaccines: WHO position paper - April 2018. Wkly Epidemiol Rec. 2018;93(16):201-220 (who-rabies-position-paper-2018.txt), Administration of rabies immunoglobulin","If category III exposure and never previously vaccinated: infiltrate rabies immunoglobulin into the wound","20 IU/kg body weight for human rabies immunoglobulin (hRIG); 40 IU/kg for equine (eRIG). Given once, at the start of the course, and infiltrated into and around the wound - not as a routine injection into a distant muscle. If not given on day 0 it may still be given up to day 7 of the vaccine course, and not after that.","A single dose, with the first vaccine dose (or up to day 7, never later)",u.lA)
B.aAF=new A.h("rectal-prolapse","Lactulose","Lactulose 3.35 g/5 mL orally: <1 year up to 5 mL/day; 1\u20136 years 5\u201310 mL/day; 7\u201314 years initially 15 mL/day, then 10\u201315 mL/day. Once daily or divided twice; adjust after 2\u20133 days.","oral.liquid",'Egyptian National Drug Formulary 2025 - Gastrointestinal Tract, lactulose monograph p119 (data/reference/text/endf-git.txt) - verbatim, adult: "Starting dose: 10-30 gm lactulose (15 \u2013 45 mL/day of oral solution)."; children 7-14 years: "Starting dose: 10 gm (15 mL of oral solution). Maintenance dose: 7-10 gm (10 \u2013 15 mL of oral solution)."; children 1-6 years: "Starting and maintenance dose: 3-7 gm (5 \u2013 10 mL of oral solution)."; infants under 1 year: "Starting and maintenance dose: 3 gm (up to 5 mL).". The indication is from Pediatric Rectal Prolapse - StatPearls (NCBI Bookshelf NBK532308) - https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK532308/ - verbatim: "osmotic agents such as polyethylene glycol, the addition of a stimulant laxative such as sennosides should be the next step in the bowel regimen. Treatment may be further escalated to bisacodyl as needed."',null,"15 to 45 mL of the oral solution a day to start (10 to 30 g), then 15 to 30 mL a day once the stool is soft","Until the child has passed stool regularly for several months with no further prolapse",u.FC)
B.azb=new A.h("rectal-prolapse","Bisacodyl","Oral, >12 years: 5\u201310 mg at bedtime. Rectal suppository, 4\u201310 years: 5 mg daily. No younger oral/rectal amounts sourced.","oral.solid",'Egyptian National Drug Formulary 2025 - Gastrointestinal Tract, bisacodyl monograph p129 (data/reference/text/endf-git.txt) - verbatim, oral: "Children over 12 years: 5 - 10 mg once daily before bedtime."; rectal: "Children 4 \u2013 10 years: 5 mg daily for immediate effect.". The place in the ladder is from Pediatric Rectal Prolapse - StatPearls (NCBI Bookshelf NBK532308) - https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK532308/ - verbatim: "osmotic agents such as polyethylene glycol, the addition of a stimulant laxative such as sennosides should be the next step in the bowel regimen. Treatment may be further escalated to bisacodyl as needed."',null,"5 to 10 mg once daily before bedtime","Short-term; the stimulant is added to the osmotic laxative, not used in its place",u.ir)
