B.ay8=new A.h("thrombophilia","Warfarin","Pediatric haematology; initial amount is not maintenance. Subsequent dosing is INR-directed.","oral.solid",'Egyptian National Blood disorders Formulary 2025, warfarin monograph - verbatim: "Initial dosage Oral: 2-10 mg, according to the patient\'s weight, age and general health", with "Maintenance dose Based on the effect of the initial dose on INR on day 3" and "Usual maintainance dose: Oral: 2-10 mg daily." When to anticoagulate indefinitely comes from the Factor V Leiden article held for this condition - verbatim: "It is highly recommended that one continue indefinite anticoagulation for unprovoked, life-threatening venous thromboembolism (VTE at an unusual location or if it is recurrent."',"Long-term oral anticoagulation, outside pregnancy","2 to 10 mg once daily initially, adjusted to the INR from day 3","Set by the specialist - indefinitely after an unprovoked, life-threatening, recurrent or unusually sited clot",u.Vp)
